WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.030
Off the coast of Queensland lies a
Marine Park of 344,400 square kilometres,

2
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.930
with about 3,000 coral reefs.

3
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.250
It has been World Heritage since 1981.

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.930
Fishing and tourism are
controlled by zoning and permits.

5
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:22.890
In 2024, the Reef Authority said the Region
continues to be well managed overall.

6
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:27.570
Yet its outlook, the same report says,
remains one of future deterioration.

7
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:32.370
How can a reef be well
managed, yet still declining?

8
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.450
In this mission, you'll trace
what people do to the Reef,

9
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.330
from 35 catchments
onshore to boats offshore.

10
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.170
Then you'll weigh up its future prospects,

11
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.330
and judge which pressures matter most.

12
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:50.020
Your mission: explain why a well-managed
reef still faces an outlook of deterioration.
